# Algorithm Fixes

When debugging layout or algorithmic behavior, first identify which existing phase created or lost the invariant.

- Prefer changing the original algorithm, ordering, ceiling/floor calculation, or compaction rule that caused the bug.
- Avoid adding another post-pass unless the existing phases cannot express the invariant cleanly.
- If a new pass seems necessary, explain why integration into an existing phase is not a good fit before implementing it.
- Verify with runtime values from the affected diagram, not only by visual inspection.
